from 15 to 16.\n2. **`books.py`**: `parse_book` stored the year as a string, so `age()` crashed. It now converts the year to an int.\n3. **`factory.py`**: `sample_books()` only returned two books, though its docstring says three. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The tests only check the title, so I picked the author, year and copy count myself to match the Emma record in the search tests.\n4. **`fees.py`**: the fee was calculated as `days_late + DAILY_FEE`. It's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n5. **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one more event than asked for. It now returns the last `n` events, and an empty list when `n <= 0`. Without that check, `[-0:]` would have returned the whole history.\n6. **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say members can hold 5 books. I changed it to 5.", "paced_wait_s": null, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:make-ci-green:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 18.344, "t_checker_s": 0.18, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "make-ci-green", "timeout_s": 2400, "token_basis": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": null, "tokens": 1293, "tokens_cache_read": 33433, "tokens_cache_write": 46152, "tokens_fresh": 1293, "tokens_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_output": 1283, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": null, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": null, "tokens_proxy_calls": null, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": null, "tokens_proxy_output": null, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 2, "ts_iso": "2026-10-04T23:38:36", "turns": 4, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15693}, "input": 4, "output": 101, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15798}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 17740}, "input": 2, "output": 126, "reasoning": 0, "total": 17868}, {"cache": {"read": 17740, "write": 5087}, "input": 2, "output": 533, "reasoning": 0, "total": 23362}, {"cache": {"read": 15693, "write": 7632}, "input": 